<title>HUNGARY: Slovenian truck protest blocks Hungarian border.</title>
<headline>Slovenian truck protest blocks Hungarian border.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenian truckers protesting against administrative backlogs blocked a border crossing with Hungary on Thursday, creating a five-km (three mile) long queue on the Hungarian side, officials said.</p>
<p>&quot;As far as we know, Slovenian truckers are protesting against slow administration on their side,&quot; Hungarian Border Police spokesman Attila Krisan told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said the Slovenian truckers had blocked the crossing at Redics, about 100 km (60 miles) northwest of Pecs. Redics is the main border crossing with Slovenia with an average daily traffic of almost 4,000 vehicles last year.</p>
<p>Krisan said Hungarian police had started to divert traffic to other checkpoints with Slovenia but those are not equipped to handle freight traffic.</p>
<p>He said trucks could reach Slovenia through Austria or Croatia.</p>
</text>
